    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119784,
      "id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $3\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $-3\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "1a425ece-3cd0-5bac-8feb-38c20614d999",
