    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $B$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $8\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-8\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "bffc9eda-b0fc-5db3-9aed-0f4327327cdc",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7c7645c2-1d6d-5260-8cdb-c5f14512d951",
