      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-1\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 1, column 2 is $1\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "f4169b60-b249-5684-960d-e8e32cb237d2",
